---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { getPage } from "../site";
---

<PageLayout page={getPage("/")}>
<div class="home-page">
  <h1 class="page-title">Quantum Computing for Complex Systems</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">
    Interactive explorations of why quantum computers offer structural advantages for modeling
    complex systems
  </p>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>
      Complex systems — from climate dynamics and biological networks to supply chains and financial
      markets — exhibit three properties that make them fundamentally difficult for classical
      computers: non-linear coupling between variables, indirect correlations that propagate through
      multi-hop networks, and rugged optimization landscapes with exponentially many local minima.
      Each of these properties maps to a capability where quantum systems may hold a structural
      advantage over classical hardware.
    </p>
    <p>
      The three interactive explainers below illustrate these properties, explain the underlying
      mathematics, and connect them to peer-reviewed research on quantum approaches to modeling
      complex systems.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <a href="/nonlinear" class="card" style="border-top-color: var(--color-primary)">
      <h2>Non-Linear Relationships</h2>
      <p>
        Why linear models break down in coupled systems — from climate tipping points to biological
        networks to financial crises — and how quantum systems model them.
      </p>
      <span class="card-arrow" style="color: var(--color-primary)">→</span></a
    ><a
      href="/hidden-correlations"

      class="card"
      style="border-top-color: var(--color-teal)"
    >
      <h2>Hidden Correlations</h2>
      <p>
        How influence propagates through intermediaries in complex networks, invisible to pairwise
        analysis.
      </p>
      <span class="card-arrow" style="color: var(--color-teal)">→</span></a
    ><a
      href="/quantum-tunneling"

      class="card"
      style="border-top-color: var(--color-coral)"
    >
      <h2>Quantum Tunneling</h2>
      <p>How quantum systems escape local minima that trap classical optimization solvers.</p>
      <span class="card-arrow" style="color: var(--color-coral)">→</span></a
    >
  </div>
</div>
</PageLayout>
